@startuml
title Assembling a modern zkSNARK, following the Marlin recipe
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  BorderColor #7A5BB5
  DiamondBackgroundColor #F3EEFB
  DiamondBorderColor #7A5BB5
  ArrowColor #7A5BB5
  StartColor #7A5BB5
  EndColor #7A5BB5
}

|Designer|
start
:pick an arithmetisation\n(R1CS, QAP or AIR);
:design a public-coin information-theoretic protocol\nin which the prover sends oracles to polynomials;
:prove soundness in the oracle model\nusing Schwartz-Zippel;

|Compiler|
:choose an extractable polynomial commitment scheme;
:replace every oracle with a commitment;
:replace every oracle query with an opening proof;
:apply Fiat-Shamir, hashing the full transcript\nto derive each verifier challenge;

|Result|
:a non-interactive argument of knowledge;
if (does the commitment need a trusted setup?) then (yes)
  :SRS-based system\nconstant proof size, pairing assumptions;
else (no)
  :transparent system\nlarger proofs, weaker assumptions;
endif
:add blinding to the committed polynomials\nto obtain zero knowledge;
stop
@enduml
